# Local tooling and data dumps — never part of the deployed site.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THIS FILE: Vercel only applies .vercelignore to CLI uploads
# (`vercel deploy`). A git-based deploy clones the repo and serves the whole `outputDirectory`,
# which for this project is "." — so everything below was still reachable on www.rdvs.studio
# (measured 2026-10-05: /scripts/build_sanity_seed.py, /studio/projects.ndjson, /studio/.env.example,
# /SANITY-SETUP.md and /fetch_behance.py all answered 200). Kept here so a manual CLI upload from a
# laptop behaves the same as production.
#
# The rule that actually protects the live site is the `routes` array in vercel.json, which answers
# 404 for these paths at the edge. If you add another tooling folder to the repo root, add a route
# for it there as well.
scripts/
scratch/
studio/
node_modules/

# Working notes and the Behance index of record.
behance_all.txt
SANITY-SETUP.md

# Credentials (already git-ignored; listed so a manual upload cannot include them).
.env
.env.local
studio/.env
studio/.env.local
studio/.env.example
